<title>USA: U.S. stocks open higher, extending gains.</title>
<headline>U.S. stocks open higher, extending gains.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wall Street shares rose at the market open on Thursday, helped by continued declines in bond yields and strength in the technology sector.</p>
<p>The Dow Industrials rose 6.50 to 8,265.81 at the start. The Nasdaq Composite rose 6.70 to 1,637.14, while the S&amp;P Index was up 1.27 at 961.59.</p>
<p>The 30-year long bond was up 7/32 at 6.47 percent yield.</p>
